WEBVTT

00:04:58.569 --> 00:05:01.464
And I'm like, "Well, I'm not sure
it didn't come to you."

00:05:01.488 --> 00:05:03.276
So that's where it all begins for me.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.510
CA: And then where it gets
even more surprising

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:08.896
is that when you say
an idea comes to people,

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:12.258
you don't just mean an idea
in the sense of a neuronal pattern

00:05:12.282 --> 00:05:13.808
of electrical activity.

00:05:13.832 --> 00:05:17.311
You literally mean something
from the outside coming in.

00:05:17.335 --> 00:05:19.165
Talk a bit more about that.

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:22.239
EG: Yeah, and the way I describe it

00:05:22.263 --> 00:05:25.626
is only the way I've
empirically experienced it,

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:29.739
which has broken down in my life
to this notion,

00:05:29.763 --> 00:05:34.236
which is that ideas are living entities.